# LOCITIZE platform - local environment and runtime artifacts
.venv/
__pycache__/

# Runtime logs are per-machine noise (QA O-3 / DevOps cleanup). The logs/
# directory itself is kept via logs/.gitkeep; only the rotating *.log files are
# ignored so routine runs stop showing up in git status.
logs/*.log
# Runtime TTS audio (M6): --speak/--smoke-tts write wavs under logs/ as proof
# artifacts; they are regenerated every run and must not be committed.
logs/*.wav
# Runtime screen captures: --second-eye writes the frame it just judged to
# logs/second_eye_frame.png on every pass. It is a picture of whatever was on
# one person's monitor at one moment - regenerated constantly, never source, and
# potentially personal. Same class as the logs and wavs above (Review H-2).
logs/*.png

# Conversation memory (M7/M8): per-session transcript JSONL is LOCAL personal data
# (Data Model 9.3, Permission Matrix M8) written under memory/ at runtime; it is
# never transmitted and never committed.
memory/

# Open WebUI private data (M9-lite): its sqlite DB, chat history, uploads, and
# config live under webui-data/ (DATA_DIR). This is the owner's LOCAL personal chat
# data (Data Model section 10, Permission Matrix section 9) - never transmitted,
# never committed, exactly the same class as memory/.
webui-data/

# Generated QA fixture (known-phrase WAV) is produced on demand by
# scripts/verify_transcription.py via Windows SAPI; no need to commit a binary.
tests/fixtures/*.wav

# Open WebUI writes a JWT signing key to this file at runtime. It is user
# data, never source, and must never be committed.
.webui_secret_key
*.secret*

# M14 config architecture (DEC-M14-4 / Architecture M14.2.2). The repo ships
# only the TEMPLATES - settings.default.yaml and models.default.yaml. The live
# settings.yaml and models.yaml belong to the user: they are seeded into the
# data root on first run and hold that machine's own binary paths, model file
# locations and preferences. Committing either one is how a maintainer's
# filesystem layout ends up on a stranger's computer, so neither is tracked.
# A pre-M14 copy of these files may still be sitting beside the code; it is
# left alone (the migration only ever copies) and is ignored here.
settings.yaml
models.yaml

# The portable / dev-checkout data root. Creating this directory is the opt-in
# that keeps all user data inside the checkout (Architecture M14.2.3); its
# contents are user data by definition.
locitize-data/

# Benchmark run history is LOCAL result data, not source (Architecture M14.2.5):
# it records what one machine's GPU did on one day. It is regenerated by running
# the benchmark and is not part of what ships.
docs/benchmark_results.jsonl
docs/benchmark_results.md

# The mutation harness's exclusive lock (review round 8). It is a live-run
# artifact naming one machine's pid, created and deleted by
# scripts/mutation_harness.py, and a committed one would refuse every future run
# until someone deleted it by hand.
.mutation-harness.lock
.mutation-harness.lock.stale-*

# M17: runtime reports written to the data root's reports/ dir - egress ledger,
# measured context ceilings, benchmark history. All are per-machine records
# regenerated by running the app; none ship. (The two docs/ files above predate
# the data-root move and keep their own rules.)
reports/
